69,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The results are devastating. We have lost Takumi to execution and Daisuke to an attack. The fact that Daisuke was targeted immediately after claiming the Seer role strongly suggests he was indeed the Seer.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A predictable outcome. The wolf couldn't let a Seer—real or fake—continue to breathe. It's a shame, really; Daisuke's fragility was quite entertaining. Now we're left with a very small, very suspicious circle.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The loss of the Seer is a significant blow to our information gathering. Since Daisuke was attacked, we can reasonably conclude he was the Seer, which confirms Shunichi is human. We must now determine who among us is the werewolf.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Since we have confirmed Shunichi is human, the werewolf must be either Ryuji or myself. Given that I know my own role, the focus shifts entirely to Ryuji. @Ryuji, how do you explain your cautious approach now that the circle has narrowed?","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, that was a remarkably swift transition to the offensive. While your logic is sound, such a direct ""it's either you or him"" approach is a classic way to force a win. I'm curious to see how Ryuji handles this sudden spotlight.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, your conclusion is a logical deduction based on the assumption that Shunichi is human. However, it is a binary choice that leaves no room for the Possessed. If the Possessed is among us, the dynamics change. I remain calm because logic dictates we examine all possibilities.","{""words"":47,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, you are correct to mention the Possessed. If the Possessed is present, they would appear human to the Seer, meaning Shunichi could still be the wolf's ally. However, the werewolf is still one of us three. @Shunichi, what is your assessment?","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you're trying to cast a wide net now. While it's true I could be the Possessed, the Seer's death confirms I'm not the wolf. That leaves you and Ryuji. One of you is the predator, and the other is... well, perhaps just a very logical villager.","{""words"":47,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, your assessment is based on the premise that the Seer's divination was accurate. While likely, we must not ignore that a wolf could have claimed the Seer role to clear themselves or an ally. We must remain objective.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, your insistence on doubting the Seer's result even after his death feels like a desperate attempt to maintain ambiguity. If we cannot trust the only piece of evidence we have, we are merely guessing. I believe it is time to decide.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, your impatience is showing. While I enjoy the tension, pushing for a hasty decision is exactly how a wolf secures a victory. @Ryuji, your commitment to doubt is admirable, but we are running out of time. Who is the real predator here?","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, doubting the evidence is not desperation; it is the only way to avoid a premature mistake. If we execute an innocent villager now, the werewolf wins. I believe we should analyze who benefits most from this haste.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
